      "math_academy_id": "q-49634",
      "knowledge_point_id": "03e934c8-da65-5615-9717-a50eee3577fd",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Other Fractional Expressions",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $u={x}^{2}+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,⟹\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u=x\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand we can solve the resulting integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(2\\sqrt{u})+C \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{u}+C \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}+C"
